   "line": 9,
   "text": "Why not a shorter block? At one twenty-eight, a loud one leaks sixty-one percent into the four's bin: the taper bought low side lobes with a main lobe twice as wide. Longer isn't the rule: two twenty-four fails, two oh eight works. What counts is where the bins land. With loud keys ten times the faint, every neighbouring tone must land at least about one point seven five bins from the bin you read. Two fifty-six gives two point two six.",
